## Database Query Optimization

### N+1 Query Prevention

```php
// ❌ BAD: N+1 query problem
$markets = Market::all();
foreach ($markets as $market) {
    echo $market->creator->name; // N queries
}

// ✅ GOOD: Eager loading
$markets = Market::with('creator')->get();
foreach ($markets as $market) {
    echo $market->creator->name; // 2 queries total
}

// ✅ GOOD: Lazy eager loading
$markets = Market::all();
$markets->load('creator');

// ✅ GOOD: Specific columns
$markets = Market::with('creator:id,name,email')->get();
```

### Efficient Queries

```php
// ✅ Select only needed columns
$markets = Market::select('id', 'name', 'status')
    ->where('status', 'active')
    ->get();

// ✅ Use chunk for large datasets
Market::chunk(100, function ($markets) {
    foreach ($markets as $market) {
        // Process market
    }
});

// ✅ Use exists() for checking existence
if (Market::where('slug', $slug)->exists()) {
    // Market exists
}

// ✅ Use count() for counting
$activeCount = Market::where('status', 'active')->count();
```

## Middleware Patterns

### Custom Middleware

```php
<?php

namespace App\Http\Middleware;

use Closure;
use Illuminate\Http\Request;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Response;

class EnsureMarketIsActive
{
    /**
     * Handle an incoming request.
     */
    public function handle(Request $request, Closure $next): Response
    {
        $market = $request->route('market');

        if ($market && !$market->isActive()) {
            return redirect()
                ->route('markets.index')
                ->with('error', 'This market is no longer active.');
        }

        return $next($request);
    }
}
```

### Registering Middleware

```php
// bootstrap/app.php
->withMiddleware(function (Middleware $middleware) {
    $middleware->alias([
        'market.active' => \App\Http\Middleware\EnsureMarketIsActive::class,
    ]);
})

// routes/web.php
Route::get('/markets/{market}/trade', [TradeController::class, 'show'])
    ->middleware(['auth', 'market.active']);
```

## Job and Queue Patterns

### Creating Jobs

```php
<?php

namespace App\Jobs;

use App\Models\Market;
use Illuminate\Bus\Queueable;
use Illuminate\Contracts\Queue\ShouldQueue;
use Illuminate\Foundation\Bus\Dispatchable;
use Illuminate\Queue\InteractsWithQueue;
use Illuminate\Queue\SerializesModels;

class CalculateMarketProbabilities implements ShouldQueue
{
    use Dispatchable, InteractsWithQueue, Queueable, SerializesModels;

    /**
     * The number of times the job may be attempted.
     */
    public int $tries = 3;

    /**
     * The number of seconds to wait before retrying the job.
     */
    public int $backoff = 10;

    /**
     * Create a new job instance.
     */
    public function __construct(
        public Market $market,
    ) {}

    /**
     * Execute the job.
     */
    public function handle(MarketService $service): void
    {
        $probabilities = $service->calculateProbabilities($this->market);

        $this->market->update([
            'current_probabilities' => $probabilities,
            'last_calculated_at' => now(),
        ]);
    }

    /**
     * Handle a job failure.
     */
    public function failed(?Throwable $exception): void
    {
        Log::error('Failed to calculate market probabilities', [
            'market_id' => $this->market->id,
            'error' => $exception->getMessage(),
        ]);
    }
}
```

### Dispatching Jobs

```php
// Dispatch immediately
CalculateMarketProbabilities::dispatch($market);

// Dispatch after delay
CalculateMarketProbabilities::dispatch($market)
    ->delay(now()->addMinutes(5));

// Dispatch to specific queue
CalculateMarketProbabilities::dispatch($market)
    ->onQueue('calculations');

// Chain jobs
CalculateMarketProbabilities::dispatch($market)
    ->chain([
        new UpdateMarketCache($market),
        new NotifySubscribers($market),
    ]);
```

## Event and Listener Pattern

### Defining Events

```php
<?php

namespace App\Events;

use App\Models\Market;
use Illuminate\Broadcasting\InteractsWithSockets;
use Illuminate\Foundation\Events\Dispatchable;
use Illuminate\Queue\SerializesModels;

class MarketCreated
{
    use Dispatchable, InteractsWithSockets, SerializesModels;

    public function __construct(
        public Market $market,
    ) {}
}
```

### Creating Listeners

```php
<?php

namespace App\Listeners;

use App\Events\MarketCreated;
use App\Notifications\NewMarketNotification;
use App\Models\User;

class NotifyAdminsOfNewMarket
{
    public function handle(MarketCreated $event): void
    {
        $admins = User::where('is_admin', true)->get();

        foreach ($admins as $admin) {
            $admin->notify(new NewMarketNotification($event->market));
        }
    }
}
```

### Registering Events

```php
// In EventServiceProvider
protected $listen = [
    MarketCreated::class => [
        NotifyAdminsOfNewMarket::class,
        UpdateMarketCache::class,
        LogMarketCreation::class,
    ],
];
```

**Remember**: Laravel patterns enable clean, maintainable, and testable backend code. Follow Laravel conventions and leverage its powerful features.
